## 🏗️ Architecture

This library follows the modular design philosophy of [lexus2k/ssd1306](https://github.com/lexus2k/ssd1306):

```
{{part}}_regs.h       Single source of truth for register definitions
     │               (No implementation, only #define and enums)
     │
     ├─→ {{part}}.h        Main API interface declarations
     │        │
     │        └─→ {{part}}.cpp     Business logic implementation
     │                 │           (Calls HAL functions, never direct I2C)
     │                 │
     │                 └─→ {{part}}_hal.cpp    Hardware Abstraction Layer
     │                              │          (Platform-specific I2C code)
     │                              │
     │                              ├─→ Arduino: Uses Wire library
     │                              └─→ Bare-metal: User implements i2c_write/read
```

### Benefits of This Architecture

1. **Maintainability**: Each file has single responsibility
2. **Portability**: Easy to add new platform support (just modify HAL)
3. **Testability**: Business logic can be tested independently
4. **Readability**: Clear separation makes code easier to understand

