## 🔧 Bare-Metal Integration

For non-Arduino platforms, you must provide I2C functions:

```cpp
// In your main.cpp or i2c_platform.cpp

extern "C" bool i2c_write(uint8_t addr, uint8_t* data, uint8_t len) {
    // Your platform-specific I2C write implementation
    // addr: 7-bit I2C address
    // data: bytes to write (first byte is register address)
    // len: number of bytes
    // Return: true if successful, false if NACK/error
}

extern "C" bool i2c_read(uint8_t addr, uint8_t* data, uint8_t len) {
    // Your platform-specific I2C read implementation
    // addr: 7-bit I2C address
    // data: buffer to store received bytes
    // len: number of bytes to read
    // Return: true if successful, false if NACK/error
}
```

See [`templates/src/{{part}}_hal.cpp.tmpl`](templates/src/{{part}}_hal.cpp.tmpl) for platform-specific examples (STM32 HAL, ESP-IDF, etc.).

